    {
      "id": "497d1cab-92aa-5c95-9e4c-2848aaed5d21",
      "name": "WhatsApp Result",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        5300,
        -100
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForEachItem",
        "jsCode": "// API acceptance is not a delivery/read receipt. Never retry an ambiguous send.\nconst response = $json.body || $json;\nconst httpStatus = $json.statusCode;\nconst messageId = response.messages?.[0]?.id;\nconst accepted = !response.error && typeof messageId === 'string' &&\n  /^wamid\\.[A-Za-z0-9_=+./:-]{1,500}$/.test(messageId);\n// Only explicit, recognized rate-limit rejections qualify for a later retry.\nconst limited = !accepted && [400, 429].includes(httpStatus) &&\n  [130429, 131056].includes(response.error?.code);\nconst rejected = !accepted && !limited && !!response.error &&\n  [400, 401, 403, 404, 405, 410, 413, 415, 422].includes(httpStatus);\nconst status = accepted ? 'submitted' : limited ? 'failed' : rejected ? 'rejected' : 'unknown';\nreturn { json: {\n  channel: 'whatsapp',\n  status,\n  error_code: accepted ? null : limited ? 'provider_rate_limited' :\n    rejected ? 'provider_rejected' : 'submission_uncertain',\n  message_id: accepted ? messageId : null,\n  automatic_retry: limited,\n  next_step: accepted\n    ? 'Check your verified test phone. Meta accepted this message; delivery and playback are not confirmed.'\n    : 'Inspect the Send WhatsApp Audio node and your test phone before any manual retry. Submission may have succeeded.'\n}};\n"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "37130ec0-50ad-5806-a366-e873b1a2c61b",
      "name": "Read Me - Test Setup",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        -480
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## WhatsApp reminders\n\nDefault: **CSV + preview + test routing**. Send mode uses a durable PostgreSQL claim and single-use reservation.\n\nFor live testing, follow **docs/whatsapp-test.md**. Use Meta's supplied test sender and your own verified recipient. Send Hello first. With window_source=webhook and backend WHATSAPP_WINDOW_SOURCE=webhook, its timestamp is recorded automatically. Manual mode still requires last_hello_at_utc.\n\nSelect the same Header Auth credential on Upload and Send: `Authorization: Bearer <token>`. Never paste the token into Demo Settings.\n\nEdit agent and bank in Demo Settings. CSV supplies customer names and dates. Set input_mode=single for Alex only.\n\nKeep institution_id stable. Submitted/unknown/submitting/rejected reminders are never automatically resent. Safe preparation failures retry on a later run, subject to backend delay/attempt limits.\n\nCustomer routing requires CSV numbers, a recent incoming message per recipient and backend WHATSAPP_CUSTOMER_ROUTING_ENABLED=true. Never use fictional CSV phones for sending.",
        "width": 660,
        "height": 380
      }
